\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O sacred head once wounded,
\par With grief and pain weighed down,
\par How scornfully surrounded
\par With thorn, Thine only crown!
\par How pale thou art with anguish,
\par With sore abuse and scorn!
\par How does that visage languish
\par Which once was bright as morn!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O Lord of Life and Glory,
\par What bliss till now was Thine!
\par I read kthe wondrous story,
\par I joy to call Thee mine.
\par Thy grief and Thy compassion
\par Were all for sinners' gain;
\par Mine, mine was the transgression,
\par But Thine the deadly pain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. What language shall I borrow 
\par To praise Thee Heavenly Friend,
\par For this Thy dying sorrow, 
\par Thy pity without end?
\par Lord, make Thine forever,
\par Nor let me faithless prove;
\par O let me never, never
\par Abuse such dying love!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Be near me, Lord, when dying;
\par O show Thyself to me;
\par And, for my succour flying,
\par Come, Lord to set me free:
\par These eyes now faith receiving,
\par From Jesus shall not move;
\par For he who dies believing
\par Dies safely through Thy love.
\par Amen
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

